LSP servers declared by extensions are discovered at startup

The CLI discovers LSP servers while it builds its config, before
Config.initialize() loads the extensions, so the LSP servers of extensions
(Claude plugins with a .lsp.json) were only found after an extension was
installed or enabled in a running session. initialize() now discovers again
once the extensions are loaded, when one of them declares LSP servers; the
discovery is not awaited, since starting a server can take long.

